invariant: INV-41
file: src/rsa_sign64.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh rsa_sign64_ifma
reason: the IFMA arm of both_powers raises the second half to the
  blinded dp in place of the blinded dq, so every signature it computes
  is wrong modulo q, and the check of INV-42 is all that keeps it from
  leaving. The rsa_sign64_ifma proof states that the kernel's exponents
  are the two it was given, every byte of each.

--- old
        rsa_ifma_sign_power_pair(m1, m1, e_p, mod_p, m2, m2, e_q, mod_q, e_len);
--- new
        rsa_ifma_sign_power_pair(m1, m1, e_p, mod_p, m2, m2, e_p, mod_q, e_len);
